# Compose interpolation: provide POSTGRES_PASSWORD, THALAMUS_WORKSPACE_DIR and
# THALAMUS_KUBECONFIG_DIR in your shell or an untracked .env file. THALAMUS_PORT
# optionally changes the loopback HTTP port (default 8080). Terminate HTTPS at
# a trusted proxy; THALAMUS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN must be its canonical HTTPS origin.
# The initial PostgreSQL password is used only when its volume is initialized.
#
# Create separate untracked .env.server and .env.worker files containing the
# respective variables below. Set actual values; do not copy example credentials.
# DATABASE_URL must reference postgres:5432, use the externally supplied
# PostgreSQL password (URL-encoded if necessary), and grant migration privileges.
# Paths inside the mounted operator workspace begin with /workspace. The
# reviewed catalog checkout must be accessible to container UID 10001; GitOps
# worktrees and repositories must also be writable by that UID.
# The worker kubeconfig is mounted from THALAMUS_KUBECONFIG_DIR/config and must
# use container-accessible certificate paths and an accessible Kubernetes API.
# Compose with the worker is a configured deployment, not the isolated local
# smoke fixture. See TESTING.md for the Docker OIDC smoke without Kubernetes.
#
# Required by both roles:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://thalamus:<url-encoded-password>@postgres:5432/thalamus
# THALAMUS_CATALOG_DIR=/workspace/<catalog-root>
#
# Required server settings:
# THALAMUS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://<public-host>
# THALAMUS_OIDC_ISSUER=https://<oidc-issuer>
# THALAMUS_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=<oidc-client-id>
# THALAMUS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret>
# THALAMUS_SESSION_SIGNING_KEY=<stable-secret-at-least-32-bytes>
# THALAMUS_PROMETHEUS_URL=https://<prometheus-endpoint>
# Optional server settings (omit rather than set empty):
# THALAMUS_GROUP_MAPPING=<json-object>
# THALAMUS_OIDC_CA_FILE=/workspace/<trusted-oidc-ca-pem>
# THALAMUS_GATEWAY_URL=https://<gateway>/v1
# THALAMUS_K8S_NAMESPACE=<namespace>
# THALAMUS_GATEWAY_CONFIGMAP=<projection-name>
# THALAMUS_WORKFLOWS_CONFIG=<operator-json>
# THALAMUS_RUNTIME_CONFIG=<operator-json>
# THALAMUS_EVIDENCE_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=<positive-seconds>
# THALAMUS_INSPECTION_CONFIG=<operator-json>
# THALAMUS_ACCESS_REPOSITORY=/workspace/<repository>
# THALAMUS_ACCESS_CATALOG_PATH=<catalog-path>
# THALAMUS_ACCESS_COMMIT=<commit>
# THALAMUS_API_INTROSPECTION_ENDPOINT=https://<introspection-endpoint>
# THALAMUS_API_CLIENT_ID=<client-id>
# THALAMUS_API_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret>
# THALAMUS_API_AUDIENCE=https://<api-resource>
# THALAMUS_API_REQUIRED_SCOPES=<space-separated-scopes>
# THALAMUS_MCP_INTROSPECTION_ENDPOINT=https://<introspection-endpoint>
# THALAMUS_MCP_CLIENT_ID=<client-id>
# THALAMUS_MCP_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret>
# THALAMUS_MCP_REQUIRED_SCOPES=<space-separated-scopes>
#
# Required worker settings:
# THALAMUS_K8S_NAMESPACE=<namespace>
# THALAMUS_GATEWAY_CONFIGMAP=<projection-name>
# THALAMUS_GATEWAY_SELECTOR_LABELS=<nonempty-json-object>
# THALAMUS_WORKER_ID=<unique-worker-id>
# THALAMUS_LEASE_NAME=<lease-name>
# THALAMUS_WORKER_HEALTH_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8081
# THALAMUS_RUNTIME_CONFIG=<same-operator-json-as-server>
# THALAMUS_RUNNERS_JSON=<operator-json>
# THALAMUS_VALIDATION_CONFIGS_JSON=<operator-json>
# THALAMUS_S3_ENDPOINT=https://<s3-endpoint>
# THALAMUS_S3_BUCKET=<bucket>
# THALAMUS_S3_REGION=<region>
# THALAMUS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<secret>
# THALAMUS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<secret>
# THALAMUS_S3_RUN_SECRET_PREFIX=<secret-name-prefix>
# THALAMUS_USAGE_PROMETHEUS_URL=https://<prometheus-endpoint>
# THALAMUS_USAGE_INPUT_COUNTER=<counter-name>
# THALAMUS_USAGE_OUTPUT_COUNTER=<counter-name>
# THALAMUS_USAGE_STEP_SECONDS=<positive-seconds>
# THALAMUS_USAGE_START_DATE=<YYYY-MM-DD>
# THALAMUS_USAGE_RETENTION_DAYS=<days>
#
# Runtime config supplies the namespace, API versions and a routes map keyed by
# published service, with public, team_id, project_id and service bindings. It
# does not enumerate candidates or pin future backend revisions. See
# deploy/install.fixture.yaml for the offline shape, not deployable values.
# Agentic observation additionally requires operator-approved exact digest
# trusted_agentic_images; an empty array disables it. Installer
# agenticSecretNames grants only named GET for immutable DB/search dependencies,
# never key projection or TLS Secrets. See README.md for the private Gateway,
# TLS, encrypted public-to-pod transport and public validation prerequisites.
#
# THALAMUS_RUNNERS_JSON is keyed by runner and includes kind, pinned image,
# command, workloads, service_account and route_target. The worker's
# THALAMUS_VALIDATION_CONFIGS_JSON is keyed by service then runner, with kind,
# route_target and approved options. The workflow runs profiles_file supplies
# service/team/project workload authorization to the server; coordinate these
# settings across server and worker. Backend identity and endpoint come from
# live observation, not these profiles.
#
# Optional worker IdP synchronization: configure exactly one source, either
# THALAMUS_IDP_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID and THALAMUS_IDP_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET, or
# THALAMUS_IDP_SNAPSHOT_FILE pointing to trusted complete snapshots. Also set
# THALAMUS_OIDC_ISSUER and the same explicit THALAMUS_GROUP_MAPPING as the
# server; THALAMUS_OIDC_CA_FILE can supply a private CA for Keycloak.
#
# GitOps workflow configuration is shared by server and worker. GitHub App
# credentials and Git transport credentials are separate; provide both
# securely when publishing. See README.md for the workflow, rollout guard,
# bucket policy, Kubernetes permissions and optional integration contracts.
